            <ArticleTitle>Dual-acting beta2 agonists/muscarinic antagonists.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1327-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1517/13543776.16.9.1327</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bifunctional aromatic derivatives that act as both beta(2) agonists and muscarinic receptor antagonists are claimed. The compounds use two separate pharmacophoric groups, coupled by a long lipohilic chain, to provide the desired biological activities and with the aim of providing a long duration of action. The compounds are claimed to be useful in the treatment of both asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and represent the first disclosure of a new concept - muscarinic antagonist-beta(2) agonists.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
